## What and why

ROAD 10: investigate chess position similarity parameterised by the aspect being studied. Add `docs/research/position-similarity.md` and link it from ROAD and a dated DONE entry.

The study covers:

- opening, pawn-structure, tactical, king-safety, piece-activity and endgame comparisons, including how these relate to the current commentary aspects;
- primary chess retrieval papers, recent expert-judgement research, conditional metric learning, ChessCLIP and ChessLM, with scope/limitations attributed;
- transparent feature distances, attack/defence graph relations behind ROAD 9, dynamic solution features and a proposed aspect-weighted baseline;
- strict metrics versus pseudometrics/relevance scores, context/symmetry handling and an aspect-specific evaluation plan.

Research and planning only: no metric/weights/encoder selected, no runtime code added and no benchmark claimed. This informs TODO 8.1/8.4/8.5/8.8; those implementation items remain open. General retrieval studies remain in #41.

This PR is based on #43 so its piece-power ROAD item and the root utility relocation underneath it remain in place. This PR's changes are ROAD.md, DONE.md and the new research note.
